From 7b818446301b6aec7f4818e2cb86b980421914dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:53:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV sessions: controls through the
 scheduler and HTTP (--reelcache-enable)

Session controls for the optional causal KV archive backend (ReelCache), Step 14:

* CausalKVSessionControlReq(op, args): plain-JSON controls dispatched by the
  scheduler to the GPU worker's backend (backend.control); typed backend
  errors become replies with code/status/message.
* In-flight controls: the backend calls a boundary hook at every clean chunk
  boundary of a session request; the scheduler polls its socket there (same
  thread), answers read-only controls at once, flags a pause of the running
  session and queues the pause first so it replies once durable; everything
  else is queued in arrival order.
* HTTP endpoints /v1/sessions..., /v1/session_capabilities,
  /v1/session_requests/{id}, /v1/session_gc, registered only with
  --reelcache-enable (the disabled server never imports the module).
* /v1/videos forwards causal_kv_session only with --reelcache-enable (400
  otherwise) and refuses client-selected paths on session requests; the
  causal stage rejects a session handle without a backend and never opens a
  run for warm-up copies.
* Session requests are never merged by dynamic batching.
* A request that restored history decodes only its new chunks by default
  (causal_kv_session.output "new"/"full", decode_context_latents warm the
  causal VAE decoder; the backend's decode plan in batch.extra["causal_kv"]).
* Seam additions: CausalKVRequest.dispatched_at (worker clock, first-new-chunk
  accounting), optional run.begin_clean_forward, observed plain requests for
  backends that set observes_plain_requests (timing only).

Disabled path unchanged: no backend, no hook, no router, no extra decode work.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
